config PON
	tristate "Passive Optical Network (PON) ONU support"
	select NET_SWITCHDEV
	help
	  The class for drivers of optical network units (ONUs), the
	  subscriber end of a passive optical network such as G-PON. It gives
	  each ONU a PON device, ponN, and three interfaces to userspace:

	  - the character device /dev/ponNomci0, through which a management
	    daemon exchanges the messages of the ONU management and control
	    interface (OMCI, ITU-T G.988) with the OLT;
	  - the "gem" link kind, one network interface for each GEM port,
	    which carries the ONU's traffic and which management creates;
	  - the "pon" generic netlink family, which reports the ONU's
	    activation state, the identifiers the OLT assigned to it, its
	    alarms and counters, and its T-CONTs.

	  A GEM interface that joins a bridge is offloaded through switchdev,
	  so the class selects it.

	  The drivers of ONU MACs select this option, so it needs setting by
	  hand only to build the class without one. If unsure, say N.

	  To compile this as a module, choose M here: the module will be
	  called pon.

config PON_OMCI_INJECT
	bool "Inject OMCI messages through debugfs"
	depends on PON && DEBUG_FS
	help
	  Give each OMCI port a debugfs file, pon/ponNomci0/inject. A write
	  to it puts one OMCI message into the port as if the MAC had received
	  it from the OLT, so that the management daemon can be tested against
	  provisioning that the OLT at hand does not send. A process that can
	  write the file can make the daemon act as if the OLT had asked for
	  anything, so the option is for test images, not for an ONU in
	  service.

	  If unsure, say N.

config PON_SIM
	tristate "Stand-in ONU MAC for testing the PON class"
	depends on PON && DEBUG_FS
	help
	  A MAC driver with no hardware, for the tests of the PON class
	  (tools/testing/selftests/drivers/net/pon/). It registers an OMCI
	  port and a data path on a platform device of its own and an
	  interface, ponsim0, that carries the traffic of GEM interfaces; the
	  state it reports is set through debugfs, in the directory pon_sim.

	  If unsure, say N.

source "drivers/net/pon/rtl9602c/Kconfig"
